      "title": "Supersaturation drives precipitation",
      "description": "Cooled, seeded pregnant liquor is supersaturated: NaAl(OH)₄ → Al(OH)₃ + NaOH. Fine seed hydrate gives surface for growth and agglomeration. Precipitation runs for roughly 30–60 h through a train of tanks, cooling from about 75–80 °C to 60–65 °C (interstage cooling raises yield). The draft-tube agitator keeps the hydrate suspended with low shear.",
